Every link opens in the system browser, and only on the user's click (Nix, on
top of nix-remote-only.patch).

Upstream v0.7.8 routes http(s) link clicks in chat markdown to a split-screen
"Web Preview" pane (a <webview>, `web-preview:navigate` event -> Chat.tsx),
and opens that pane by itself whenever a browser/web tool event carries a URL
(useChatIPC.ts). This patch:
  - markdown links: always window.hermesAPI.openExternal (main's audited
    openExternalUrl -> shell.openExternal), from the user's click;
  - the tool-event auto-open is gone, and nothing listens for
    `web-preview:navigate` any more (an event is not a click);
  - the pane, its globe toggle button and the inspect hook are removed from
    Chat, and the main window gets webviewTag: false (nothing else in the
    app mounts a <webview>; Office uses an in-renderer 3D view).
Tested by src/renderer/src/components/AgentMarkdown.links-external.test.tsx.

